language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ three_sum: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Given a collection of integers, find exactly m elements that sum to zero.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `three_sum.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/three_sum.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `three_sum_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py three_sum.json
$   savilerow model.eprime three_sum_1.param -run-solver

$ number of integers in the collection, derived from the data: the length of nums (not a field of the reader's JSON)
given nums_dim1 : int
letting n = nums_dim1
$ nums[i]: the i-th integer of the collection, indices 1-based (the data's index 0 is nums[1])
given nums : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int
$ how many elements must be selected
given m : int

$ indices[i]: element i of the collection is selected
find indices : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of bool

such that
$ exactly m elements are selected
(sum i : int(1..n) . toInt(indices[i])) = m,
$ the selected elements sum to zero
(sum i : int(1..n) . toInt(indices[i]) * nums[i]) = 0
